     "problem_md": "The symbol for an atom of iron is shown:\n\n`F presubscript 26 presuperscript 56 e`\n\nDeduce the number of electrons and the number of neutrons in this atom.\n\nelectrons: ..................\n\nneutrons: ..................",
     "solution_md": "> **[mark-scheme]**\n> - Electrons: 26 **[1 mark]**\n> - Neutrons: 30 **[1 mark]**\n\n> **[exam-tip]**\n> Electrons = proton (atomic) number for a neutral atom; neutrons = mass number minus proton number (56 − 26 = 30)."
